{
  "type": "doc",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Database readers may also need source-IP limits: grant necessary privileges, but allow use only from a defined network."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I tried QueryPie’s "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Allowed Zone"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", retaining the same user/read privileges while changing allowed IPs, then restoring them and checking access again."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Finding the Current IP in Access History"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I created the lab connection "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "DB Allowed Zone Lab"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", reused the MySQL orders, and granted Demo Developer "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Read-Only"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " access."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Before defining IPs, I connected in the web editor and opened "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Audit → DB Access History"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " to inspect user, connection, route, and Client IP "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "172.21.0.1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-ip-restrictions/01.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 1. User and Client IP in the new connection’s access history.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 1. User and Client IP in the new connection’s access history."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Using the address actually recorded by QueryPie clarified which IP to register."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Applying Allowed IPs Only to This Connection"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "General → Company Management → Allowed Zones"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " I created a new Zone in this menu, named "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "EP40 - DB Client Zone"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", with IP range "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "172.21.0.1/32"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". /32 specifies one IPv4 address."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-ip-restrictions/02.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 2. Dedicated Zone permitting the current IP alone.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 2. Dedicated Zone permitting the current IP alone."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I selected it in DB Allowed Zone Lab → Allowed Zone and saved. The Zone’s applied-resource list contained only this connection."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-ip-restrictions/03.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 3. Dedicated allowed range assigned to the database connection.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 3. Dedicated allowed range assigned to the database connection."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Named Zones are selected per connection, making both the applied range and affected databases easy to inspect."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A new developer connection queried order 27002 and returned "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "SHIPPED, 18500.00"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " as one row. Including the current IP allowed normal use."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-ip-restrictions/04.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 4. Order query succeeds while the IP is allowed.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 4. Order query succeeds while the IP is allowed."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Read Privileges Alone Are Not Enough"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "After disconnecting, I changed only the same Zone’s range to "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "192.0.2.254/32"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", a documentation address used to exclude the real IP. I neither changed users nor revoked Read-Only."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-ip-restrictions/05.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 5. Same database and privileges; only the Zone’s allowed IP changes.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 5. Same database and privileges; only the Zone’s allowed IP changes."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Connect now stopped before opening SQL and displayed the following."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "“This database is not accessible by this network zone.”"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The current network Zone could not access the database. Read-Only and Active remained visible behind the prompt, showing that "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "the connection’s IP condition also applied."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-ip-restrictions/06.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 6. A new connection outside the allowed range is denied despite Read-Only.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 6. A new connection outside the allowed range is denied despite Read-Only."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Restoring the IP Restores the Same Query"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I restored the Zone’s original range "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "172.21.0.1/32"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", without regranting privileges or changing database accounts."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A new developer connection returned 27002, SHIPPED, 18500.00 again. The user and privileges stayed fixed while IP settings governed connectivity."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-ip-restrictions/07.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 7. Original IP restored; same SQL returns the same order.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 7. Original IP restored; same SQL returns the same order."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The comparison changed the allowlist from the same environment. Each step disconnected and established a fresh connection."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The Denial Reason Remains in History"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "DB Access History showed Success, Failure, Success as the IP was included, excluded, then restored, all with matching user, database, and Client IP."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The failed record’s Error Message included "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "the current IP and the explanation that it could not access this database"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", matching what the user saw."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/database-ip-restrictions/08.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 8. Failed connection retains IP and denial reason.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 8. Failed connection retains IP and denial reason."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Both permitted SELECTs also succeeded in Query Audit. Connection history explains access decisions; SQL audits explain executed work."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I liked "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "managing both who may query and from which IP they may connect"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". Necessary privileges remain while each connection has defined network boundaries, with outcomes and reasons recorded for operators."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This lab used QueryPie Community 11.6.7 and MySQL 8.0.42 with test users and orders."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Reference: "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "link",
